{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage","id":1432470,"title":"Non-Dragon-Blooded on the Caul Pilgrimage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-17T01:03:25-08:00","id":1432470,"title":"Non-Dragon-Blooded on the Caul Pilgrimage","content":"What ideas (motivations and/or effects) do you have for non-Terrestrial Exalts following the Caul pilgrimage road? I introduced an Abyssal NPC in tonight's session, and I'm thinking about making the Caul pilgrimage the way to redeem her into a Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T02:06:58-08:00","id":1432475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage#post1432470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What ideas (motivations and/or effects) do you have for non-Terrestrial Exalts following the Caul pilgrimage road? I introduced an Abyssal NPC in tonight's session, and I'm thinking about making the Caul pilgrimage the way to redeem her into a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple.<br /> <br /> Assasination, kidnapping, or robbing of any pilgrims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T02:35:14-08:00","id":1432477,"title":"","content":"I think the Caul rewards should be tailored to the specific needs of the campaign. I really don't see how the power of Lunar and Gaia would redeem an Abyssal into a Solar - but I do see how it might turn them into something else. Here's my spitball ideas:<br /> <br /> Lunars: Gain the Charm Moon-and-Earth Marriage, ignoring the prerequisites. All their children with their Terrestrial Mate will be born Moon-Touched and blessed by Gaia (Awakened Essence, Exalted Healing, Well Bred) if not Exalted as Dragon-Blooded. Additionally ignore Anima Flux as if the Lunar was a Dragon-Blooded. The Caul is a norishing place celebrating the love between Gaia and Luna - it's not going to grant &quot;kill DB powers&quot;. If the Black Lion succeeds in corrupting all the holy sites on the Caul to make them hostile to Dragon-Blooded, the island breaks into pieces and sinks beneath the sea, lost forever.<br /> <br /> Solars: I likely see this as part of a Legendary Social Goal - maybe to heal the rift between Lunars and Dragon-Blooded, if only on the Caul. I could probably see it granting some kind of virtual audience with Gaia and Luna to commune with them. Maybe an Eclipse-style enforced cease-fire on the Caul.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I see completing the pilgrimage on the &quot;Lunar side&quot; granting the ability to transform somehow. Such as a transgender Solar getting to alter their body as they see fit. <i>Or</i> granting the ability to shapeshift into a (single animal) spirit shape.<br /> <br /> Completing the pilgrimage on the &quot;Dragon-Blooded&quot; side might grant the ability to enter Elemental Aura (only really useful for Immaculate Martial Arts, but there it is). <i>Or </i>immunity to Anima Flux as if the Solar was a Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> The Caul isn't for Solars. I don't have a problem with Solars playing here, but it's not their patrons and their legacy. They're outsiders. And the reward they get, if any, should reflect that. If a Solar wants to to it &quot;for teh lulz&quot; then I'm absolutely okay with the pilgrimage either giving them nothing or straight-up killing them. But if they approach the pilgrimage <i>as a pilgrimage </i>with proper reverence, they should get <i>something</i>. But it should be <i>one thing</i>, <i>probably </i>one thing they could get through other methods (like Sorcery), and definitely one thing less (directly) valuable (to them personally) than if a Lunar or Dragon-Blooded did the pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> Sidereals: The reward should be strange and unknowable. In all the time the Dragon-Blooded have held the Cault, I feel like a Sidereal would have tried, but I feel like that shouldn't help anyone actually know what happened.<br /> <br /> Liminals: I could genuinely see this making them truly &quot;alive&quot;. What this means is going to depend on what exactly &quot;alive&quot; means in your Liminal game but you won't be &quot;liminal&quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> Abyssals: I don't see Solar redemption. I do see some kind of transformation from an undead Exalt with power over death to a living Exalt with power over night.<br /> <br /> Infernals: No idea. (I can see Infernals destroying the Caul.)<br /> <br /> Heroic Mortals: Death and rebirth as one of the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> God-Blooded: Elevation to god-hood.<br /> <br /> Elemental: Elevation to Lesser Elemental Dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T03:30:22-08:00","id":1432479,"title":"","content":"Now this is awkward...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T04:01:21-08:00","id":1432482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432477#post1432477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Caul rewards should be tailored to the specific needs of the campaign. I really don't see how the power of Lunar and Gaia would redeem an Abyssal into a Solar - but I do see how it might turn them into something else. Here's my spitball ideas:<br /> <br /> Lunars: Gain the Charm Moon-and-Earth Marriage, ignoring the prerequisites. All their children with their Terrestrial Mate will be born Moon-Touched and blessed by Gaia (Awakened Essence, Exalted Healing, Well Bred) if not Exalted as Dragon-Blooded. Additionally ignore Anima Flux as if the Lunar was a Dragon-Blooded. The Caul is a norishing place celebrating the love between Gaia and Luna - it's not going to grant &quot;kill DB powers&quot;. If the Black Lion succeeds in corrupting all the holy sites on the Caul to make them hostile to Dragon-Blooded, the island breaks into pieces and sinks beneath the sea, lost forever.<br /> <br /> Solars: I likely see this as part of a Legendary Social Goal - maybe to heal the rift between Lunars and Dragon-Blooded, if only on the Caul. I could probably see it granting some kind of virtual audience with Gaia and Luna to commune with them. Maybe an Eclipse-style enforced cease-fire on the Caul.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I see completing the pilgrimage on the &quot;Lunar side&quot; granting the ability to transform somehow. Such as a transgender Solar getting to alter their body as they see fit. <i>Or</i> granting the ability to shapeshift into a (single animal) spirit shape.<br /> <br /> Completing the pilgrimage on the &quot;Dragon-Blooded&quot; side might grant the ability to enter Elemental Aura (only really useful for Immaculate Martial Arts, but there it is). <i>Or </i>immunity to Anima Flux as if the Solar was a Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> The Caul isn't for Solars. I don't have a problem with Solars playing here, but it's not their patrons and their legacy. They're outsiders. And the reward they get, if any, should reflect that. If a Solar wants to to it &quot;for teh lulz&quot; then I'm absolutely okay with the pilgrimage either giving them nothing or straight-up killing them. But if they approach the pilgrimage <i>as a pilgrimage </i>with proper reverence, they should get <i>something</i>. But it should be <i>one thing</i>, <i>probably </i>one thing they could get through other methods (like Sorcery), and definitely one thing less (directly) valuable (to them personally) than if a Lunar or Dragon-Blooded did the pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> Sidereals: The reward should be strange and unknowable. In all the time the Dragon-Blooded have held the Cault, I feel like a Sidereal would have tried, but I feel like that shouldn't help anyone actually know what happened.<br /> <br /> Liminals: I could genuinely see this making them truly &quot;alive&quot;. What this means is going to depend on what exactly &quot;alive&quot; means in your Liminal game but you won't be &quot;liminal&quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> Abyssals: I don't see Solar redemption. I do see some kind of transformation from an undead Exalt with power over death to a living Exalt with power over night.<br /> <br /> Infernals: No idea. (I can see Infernals destroying the Caul.)<br /> <br /> Heroic Mortals: Death and rebirth as one of the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> God-Blooded: Elevation to god-hood.<br /> <br /> Elemental: Elevation to Lesser Elemental Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We kind of know what the Dragonblooded end does. It's that their next child will definetly be exalted.<br /> For the Lunar end, I agree it's not going to be &quot;murder all the Dragonblooded&quot; powers--I'd probably go with &quot;Can change their Totem Spirit&quot; or something more inward facing. Well Bred is a social merit at this point, so that's...odd for a sign of Gaia's blessing. Thematically, Lunars just aren't about legacy and family lines the way dragons are--that should be reflected in the &quot;reward&quot; for completing the pilgrimage.<br /> Black Lion claiming all sites won't sink the island, just as the Dragonblooded claiming all sites won't--It's a place celeberating Gaia and Luna's love, not the Dragons and Luna, and certainly not the Dragonblooded and the Lunars. That and I kinda find the idea of &quot;if the Black Lion SUCCEEDS he'll destroy everything he loves&quot; kinda...undercutting his character and making him a boring extremist.<br /> Elementals might get something. But that's it. The other Exalts have no reason to regard the Caul as a holy place for them--Mount Meru is probably better, or a lost First Age temple to the Sun or something similair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 01-17-2021, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T05:31:30-08:00","id":1432485,"title":"","content":"I'm referring specifically to stuff like:<br /> <br /> &quot;Third Daughter of the Leaves took Garianghis, and she holds it now for her own, having slain citizens that couldn\u2019t escape. [...] she contents herself with strange rituals that, rumor has it, are intended to poison the dreams of what few Dragon-Blooded remain in the Caul.&quot;<br /> &quot;She cares little for it herself, concerned more with obscure rituals she believes could use Garianghis\u2019 power to imprison every Dragon-Blood on the Caul in ceaseless nightmare.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sandswept Garda-Empress means to use the memory of Sekima as a weapon and has spent more time within it than any other. The deeper her connections to Sekima\u2019s people grow, the more she lays her plans against whatever future pilgrims may trespass here. Woe betide such unfortunates, for if she\u2019s successful, the memory of Sekima will become a living hell, aggressive and unwelcoming.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Not just the Lunars holding all the shrines, that would be fine.<br /> <br /> And Well Bred does increase the chances of your kids Exalting.<br /> <br /> I think changing your totem spirit is fine, but why would you want to?<br /> <br /> I think the other Exalts don't need anything from doing the pilgrimage, by default. But if you want to run a story about other Exalts doing the pilgrimage... then it should do something?<br /> <br /> Like, by default, the Reclaimation can't happen. But if you want to run a story about the Reclaimation happening, then I'll give you ideas as to what might happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-19-2021, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T05:39:11-08:00","id":1432487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432482#post1432482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We kind of know what the Dragonblooded end does. It's that their next child will definetly be exalted.<br /> For the Lunar end, I agree it's not going to be &quot;murder all the Dragonblooded&quot; powers--I'd probably go with &quot;Can change their Totem Spirit&quot; or something more inward facing. Well Bred is a social merit at this point, so that's...odd for a sign of Gaia's blessing. Thematically, Lunars just aren't about legacy and family lines the way dragons are--that should be reflected in the &quot;reward&quot; for completing the pilgrimage.<br /> Black Lion claiming all sites won't sink the island, just as the Dragonblooded claiming all sites won't--It's a place celeberating Gaia and Luna's love, not the Dragons and Luna, and certainly not the Dragonblooded and the Lunars. That and I kinda find the idea of &quot;if the Black Lion SUCCEEDS he'll destroy everything he loves&quot; kinda...undercutting his character and making him a boring extremist.</div> </div> </div> </div>What JohnDoe244 described &quot;<i>if the Black Lion succeeds in corrupting all the holy sites on the Caul to make them hostile to Dragon-Blooded</i>&quot; seems to go <i><b>considerably </b></i>beyond claiming all the holy sites and seems to point out to quite different readings of the elder's character and intentions, ihmo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432482#post1432482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elementals might get something. But that's it. The other Exalts have no reason to regard the Caul as a holy place for them--Mount Meru is probably better, or a lost First Age temple to the Sun or something similair.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's holy either way and that on itself as in &quot;a place touched by the divinity and where they might be more attentive to the acts or words of mortal beings&quot;, what might be special enough in a number of games, even if the history behind the place's holiness if not directly resonant with the nature of other exalts. Just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T06:07:05-08:00","id":1432488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432485#post1432485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm referring specifically to stuff like:<br /> <br /> And Well Bred does increase the chances of your kids Exalting.<br /> <br /> I think changing your totem spirit is fine, but why would you want to?<br /> <br /> I think the other Exalts don't need anything from doing the pilgrimage, by default. But if you want to run a story about other Exalts doing the pilgrimage... then it should do something?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well Bred...doesn't? I don't think it does--oh huh. I swore 3e fixed it and made it clear that it was _just_ a social pedigree. I'm a tad disappointed now, adding that to the list of houseruled ones--the benefits to resolve and reputation seemed more than enough for that.<br /> Changing your totem spirit was the only thing I could think of for lunars, because I think it's wierd to focus on their offspring for it. I admit, I'm disappointed the Lunars book didn't address it, and hope that the Kickstarter book does.<br /> As for the last point and Baldaam's...I mean, it is a holy site in that a divinity walked there, but I disagree that they should get something from it beyond the spiritual experience of a pilgrimage. You can make that a story, that in it of itself might be fine--and I agree with the notion of an audience with Luna or something, but I don't think it deserves a mechanical reward no. That's a point of ST divergence I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 01-17-2021, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T06:27:34-08:00","id":1432489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432488#post1432488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well Bred...doesn't? I don't think it does--oh huh. I swore 3e fixed it and made it clear that it was _just_ a social pedigree. I'm a tad disappointed now, adding that to the list of houseruled ones--the benefits to resolve and reputation seemed more than enough for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you propose to have a version of the Dragon Blooded in which there are no fluctuations to the potential for Exalted children based on family history, but there is still a metric by which one is a more or less desirable marriage prospect based on... what, exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T07:06:25-08:00","id":1432494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432488#post1432488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Bred...doesn't? I don't think it does--oh huh. I swore 3e fixed it and made it clear that it was _just_ a social pedigree.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Well-bred merit states that the children are significantly more likely to exalt. What it does not do is give hard numbers on that.<br /> <br /> Should it come up, it will be a narrative decision as to whether or not a character's children exalt; not something left to a roll of the dice. (See the Breeding and Exaltation box on page 143.)<br /> <br /> The only mechanical bonus given are on those bargaining dice rolls. It is fine as it stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 01-17-2021, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T07:12:32-08:00","id":1432496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432489#post1432489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you propose to have a version of the Dragon Blooded in which there are no fluctuations to the potential for Exalted children based on family history, but there is still a metric by which one is a more or less desirable marriage prospect based on... what, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>I rewrote this a few times to elucidate my discomfort percisely.<br /> I'm fine with the inherent dragonblooded idea that dragonblooded tend to exalt on lineage, and that &quot;two dbs are more likely to have a db child than a db and a mortal&quot;.<br /> I'm not okay with there being a significant difference between dragonblooded, to the degree as to provide a meaningful merit. I preferred the merit when it represented the social mythology that you had a higher chance of an exalted child, not when it was a fact.<br /> <br /> The idea that a scion of a great house, who's father and mother and both sets of grandparents and all four sets of great-grand parents all exalted, being more likely to have an exalted child than an Outcaste who's last exalted relation was 5 centuries ago should be a social fiction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432494#post1432494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Well-bred merit states that the children are significantly more likely to exalt. What it does not do is give hard numbers on that.<br /> <br /> Should it come up, it will be a narrative decision as to whether or not a character's children exalt; not something left to a roll of the dice. (See the Breeding and Exaltation box on page 143.)<br /> <br /> The only mechanical bonus given are on those bargaining dice rolls. It is fine as it stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically it's fine. I just find the sidebar unneccessary and the statement at the start of the merit uncomfortable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 01-17-2021, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T07:25:27-08:00","id":1432500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432496#post1432496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not okay with there being a significant difference between dragonblooded</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that does dramatically change the entire dynamic of House Nellens in particular, and really the whole Scarlet Dynasty. Does House Mnemon have no reputation for good breeding?<br /> <br /> Not to mention it means portraying outcastes as just as capable of producing Exalted children as anybody else, which ought to dramatically increase their numbers in the Threshold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I preferred the merit when it represented the social mythology that you had a higher chance of an exalted child, not when it was a fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's never been the Merit or Background.<br /> <br /> The only reversal of this kind was with leftover children, and that one actually did go in the direction of &quot;being leftover detracts from bloodline&quot; to that being an untested misconception of the Dynasty.<br /> <br /> I presume you're stating that the Merit would represent a bonus to marriage negotiations based on a complete misconception, but there are setting implications dotted all over the Realm based on Exaltation rates being a thing of much concern that is heavily documented and speculated upon. To keep that social quality while removing its actual basis is to portray the Dynasty as, well, very stupid.<br /> <br /> As for the sidebar, I for one am grateful to have for once given <i>some</i> basis for what the ratio of Exalted to unExalted Dynasts is, compared to previous Editions in which it's an important question whose answer is completely up in the air. To have been told how many children on average they have but an awkward shrug for the matter of how many of them were even Dragon Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-17-2021, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T07:28:09-08:00","id":1432501,"title":"","content":"Doing the Caul pilgrimage is far more significant than the well bred merit. It guarantees that your next kid will exalt. That's as whole lot beyond &quot;likely to exalt&quot; to me. Obviously the pilgrimage would mean even more to someone with a lesser pedigree. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking that the pilgrimage for Lunars would grant them access to some benefit register to shape shifting. I'm thinking a hearts blood form unobtainable any other way. Maybe some boost to their spirit shape that can't be replicated with charms? I dunno I'm spitballing but it should be something that's lunar specific. To me that means shape shifting.<br /> <br /> For other exalt type that make the pilgrimage they get a slow clap and a thumbs up. The Caul isn't about other exalts and that's ok. There's plenty that a group can get done in the Caul that doesn't involve actually going on the pilgrimage. Same is true of Lunars and DB. No one should NEED to go on the pilgrimage to make the Caul a worthwhile setting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T07:29:27-08:00","id":1432502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432500#post1432500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume you're stating that the Merit would represent a bonus to marriage negotiations based on a complete misconception, but there are setting implications dotted all over the Realm based on Exaltation rates being a thing of much concern that is heavily documented and speculated upon. To keep that social quality while removing its actual basis is to portray the Dynasty as, well, very stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more than happy for the Dynasts to have promoted a mythology that concentrates power into a handful of families &quot;for the sake of keeping the blood pure&quot;, when that is in fact not actually metaphysically supported and is maintained for the same reason any eugenics based colonial empire of aristocrats promote such a belief system. So...Yes? Yes. I <i>personally </i> find that more interesting than there actually being a difference between Mnemnon and Nellens exaltation rates.<br /> <br /> Edit: AS for rate of Outcastes, yeah, I don't mind there being a large number of non-realm dragonblooded families, with the Realm's larger share coming from active efforts to incorporate existing states and recruit lost eggs more than their actual eugencis program having any validity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 01-17-2021, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T07:30:49-08:00","id":1432504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432501#post1432501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing the Caul pilgrimage is far more significant than the well bred merit. It guarantees that your next kid will exalt. That's as whole lot beyond &quot;likely to exalt&quot; to me. Obviously the pilgrimage would mean even more to someone with a lesser pedigree.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Well Bred merit came up when it was suggested that the child of a Lunar who completed the pilgrimage would recieve that merit among others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T07:33:14-08:00","id":1432505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432504#post1432504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Well Bred merit came up when it was suggested that the child of a Lunar who completed the pilgrimage would recieve that merit among others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I don't think that makes sense though. The Caul is a place of both Luna and Gaia. The DB who do the pilgrimage don't get any benefits related to Lunars, why would the reverse be true?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T08:26:14-08:00","id":1432509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432500#post1432500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's never been the Merit or Background.</div> </div> </div> </div>We wish this was so. Rolling to see if your child exalted was a terrible idea, but it was there.<br /> <br /> Manual of Exalted Power: Dragonblooded did include bonuses for the roll in the Breeding Background. It just took Scroll of Errata to find out what this actually entailed. Scroll of Heros also included other means of boosting the roll. So this...<br /> <br /> Ugh. This spawned <i>dragonblooded army breeding camp</i> plans on game discussion boards. <br /> <br /> Let us never do that again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T08:48:45-08:00","id":1432511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432501#post1432501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing the Caul pilgrimage is far more significant than the well bred merit. It guarantees that your next kid will exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeap. But only the next. So significant but limited.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432501#post1432501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's as whole lot beyond &quot;likely to exalt&quot; to me. Obviously the pilgrimage would mean even more to someone with a lesser pedigree.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a nice story benefit. No direct mechanical advantage, but plenty of plot hook potential.<br /> <br /> That, I think, is a good goalpost.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432501#post1432501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one should NEED to go on the pilgrimage to make the Caul a worthwhile setting</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 01-17-2021, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T09:10:50-08:00","id":1432519,"title":"","content":"Seeing the sights of the Caul seems like a good reason to do the Pilgramage regardless of what one's exaltation or lack thereof is. Plus I mean its a territory in Creation that got dissolved by the Wyld and then came back, that seems like a worthwhile reason to go there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T15:58:12-08:00","id":1432549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage#post1432470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What ideas (motivations and/or effects) do you have for non-Terrestrial Exalts following the Caul pilgrimage road? I introduced an Abyssal NPC in tonight's session, and I'm thinking about making the Caul pilgrimage the way to redeem her into a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that it\u2019s your game and you can do what you want, I don\u2019t think an Abyssal should find redemption on the Caul. Creation is a big place, and the Caul is literally one corner of it that happens to be hyper-focused on Dragonbloods and Lunars. You can always introduce another location more tailored and suited for Abyssal redemptions.<br /> <br /> With that said, I like the idea of an Abyssal BELIEVING the Caul might hold hope for them. Shadowlands have difficulty manifesting on the continent, so an Abyssal\u2019s arrival would be a dire circumstance set to disrupt the war going on there.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not a bad story idea but I wouldn\u2019t have an Abyssal find salvation there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T17:09:53-08:00","id":1432557,"title":"","content":"Okay, moving on.<br /> <br /> If it was me, other Exalted undertaking the Caul pilgrimage wouldn't bestow any form of powers, but would have a very good chance of bestowing that person with a deep insight into the Lunars or Terrestrials that could be used to relate to them in unique ways.<br /> <br /> I think I'd represent that as a Merit with at least some particular social bonus; perhaps something like the equivalent of a virtual Intimacy that can be extended to any of the respective Exalted type, but one with a relatively narrow and esoteric scope. Say, something that can appeal to them on grounds of the spiritual and metaphysical. Possibly leveraging into things like the role bonuses of their Castes and Aspects.<br /> <br /> So like, you could appeal to a Dragon Blood to conduct themselves in some manner fitting to what could be the overall mission statement of the Terrestrial Exalted, or their place in the world. Conversely, the person's insight of that kind means that they themselves can be appealed to on similar grounds. It's not the direct transformation that comes from having the appropriately compatible Essence, but there's something profound about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T17:11:28-08:00","id":1432558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432509#post1432509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We wish this was so. Rolling to see if your child exalted was a terrible idea, but it was there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, why are you saying this to me? What part of the section of text quoted above that statement made you think I was saying anything to do with that side of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T19:04:37-08:00","id":1432570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432487#post1432487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What JohnDoe244 described &quot;<i>if the Black Lion succeeds in corrupting all the holy sites on the Caul to make them hostile to Dragon-Blooded</i>&quot; seems to go <i><b>considerably </b></i>beyond claiming all the holy sites and seems to point out to quite different readings of the elder's character and intentions, ihmo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's more in line with what Third Daughter of the Leaves is trying to accomplish. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T22:37:40-08:00","id":1432580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432509#post1432509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We wish this was so. Rolling to see if your child exalted was a terrible idea, but it was there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The discussion was referring to the Well-Bred Merit, not the Breeding Background. There's never been an iteration of the Well-Bred Merit that had you roll to see if your kid Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-18T18:35:49-08:00","id":1432644,"title":"","content":"At the risk of sounding trite: Because it's there? Think about it from the perspective of a Solar with, for the sake of argument, no investment in any specific belief system in which the Caul plays a central role. You've heard the Realm really badly wants this strange, foreign land. You've heard the Lunars regard it as sacred. And you've heard weird, but nonlethal things happen to you just to complete the journey.<br /> <br /> Even if Solar Joe doesn't actually get anything out of the Caul, he might take some interest in the burning landscapes and the city that can only be traversed in dreams and all the other mystic scenery as he wanders from scenic vista to scenic vista. Depending on how you play it this could be a chance for the Solar's player to reflect on the legacy left behind by previous civilisations and wonder how their own character's goals compare. Or for the sorcerously inclined, even if the place has little to do with their own understanding of magic it might be a good place to get some artistic inspiration for their own magic. Or it can be an actual vacation.<br /> <br /> For your Abyssal, it could well be that despite having no direct connection with your patron the Caul is intrinsically wondrous and soothing in a weird way that it brings you to a calming state of mind in which redemption is easier than it would normally be. I could also see an Infernal just having a fun time trying to play around with the phenomena of the Caul using her powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","user":"Organ Boy","date":". 01-18-2021, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T01:46:51-08:00","id":1432662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432580#post1432580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The discussion was referring to the Well-Bred Merit, not the Breeding Background. There's never been an iteration of the Well-Bred Merit that had you roll to see if your kid Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Breeding Background <i>was</i> the previous iteration of the Well-Bred merit (and Thin-Blooded flaw).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T03:48:27-08:00","id":1432668,"title":"","content":"Person A: I liked it better when it represented a social mythology.<br /> Person B: But it never did that.<br /> Person C: Um actually, it <i>did</i> include rolling to see if your child Exalted.<br /> Person B: {withers away to dust}<br /> <br /> Unless I've misread, and &quot;we wish this was so&quot; was a not particularly clear way of saying one wished it was the purely social matter it has never once been. A straightforward way of reading the following sentence would be that there was a misconception, but I could just about see it as a way of reinforcing why the desire was for it to be social, rather than a citation to prove somebody incorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T07:20:40-08:00","id":1432681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage#post1432470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What ideas (motivations and/or effects) do you have for non-Terrestrial Exalts following the Caul pilgrimage road? I introduced an Abyssal NPC in tonight's session, and I'm thinking about making the Caul pilgrimage the way to redeem her into a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be a bit simplistic, but you could always lean into the old 'past life' trope? Make it more personal rather than fret about creating a splat-wide mechanic?<br /> <br /> Maybe your Abyssal escorted their Lunar mate on the pilgrimage in days gone by and the Abyssal is being pulled to relive that experience and remember who they were? Or maybe their Lunar mate asked to be buried on the Caul long ago and, grief-stricken, the Abyssal elected to bury their own treasured daiklave with them. Now the tomb, the location of which can only be found via visions granted to someone who has completed the pilgrimage, has just been disturbed and the daiklave is in the hands of another \u2013 flooding your Abyssal with flashes of rememberance of the person who they used to be.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps your Abyssal led a particularly valiant and pious gens of DBs in a mighty battle battle against a Fae incursion. The DBs sacrificed themselves and the site of their heroic last stand has just been desecrated by Lunar forces. Compelled by forces they do not quite understand, the Abyssal undertakes to complete the pilgrimage in order to cleanse the site, in the process taking another faltering step towards redemption.<br /> <br /> Etc etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 01-19-2021, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T20:27:42-08:00","id":1432746,"title":"","content":"I think it might be cool if an Abyssal's redemption quest involved learning from the magic of the different types of Exalted, for which the Caul pilgrimage handles &quot;learning from&quot; Lunars, DBs, or both, but who also has to go on an incredibly difficult quest to a location important to Solars, an incredibly difficult quest to a location important to Sidereals, and maybe some others. Like needing help from all your friends to redeem yourself, but on a more cosmic scale.<br /> <br /> I also think what Moss said is very cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T03:46:10-08:00","id":1432770,"title":"","content":"Perhaps an Abyssal or Infernal's Limit trait being altered would be an interesting potential reward for pursuing the Caul, at least their Limit Triggers if not their Limit Breaks.<br /> <br /> I could see an Abyssal's being more flavored by Luna in their role as guardian of thresholds with different Triggers and loss of the Whispers trait. I could also see an Infernal's might be more flavored by Gaia being a primordial that wasn't filled with anger tempering the Exaltation's thirst for revenge, potentially altering the nature of the Coadjutor or adding an Anima Flux, the Yozis are still kin to her after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T05:29:23-08:00","id":1432774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432502#post1432502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more than happy for the Dynasts to have promoted a mythology that concentrates power into a handful of families &quot;for the sake of keeping the blood pure&quot;, when that is in fact not actually metaphysically supported and is maintained for the same reason any eugenics based colonial empire of aristocrats promote such a belief system. So...Yes? Yes. I <i>personally </i> find that more interesting than there actually being a difference between Mnemnon and Nellens exaltation rates.<br /> <br /> Edit: AS for rate of Outcastes, yeah, I don't mind there being a large number of non-realm dragonblooded families, with the Realm's larger share coming from active efforts to incorporate existing states and recruit lost eggs more than their actual eugencis program having any validity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Terrestrial Exaltation is explicitly hereditary. Ex. Pli. Cit. Ly. To the best of my knowledge, it has never been otherwise. The idea that the number of Dragon-Blooded in your ancestry actually has no effect on the likelihood of your own Exaltation doesn't just make no sense; it makes <i>negative</i> sense. It actively creates a plot hole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T06:08:48-08:00","id":1432775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432502#post1432502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more than happy for the Dynasts to have promoted a mythology that concentrates power into a handful of families &quot;for the sake of keeping the blood pure&quot;, when that is in fact not actually metaphysically supported and is maintained for the same reason any eugenics based colonial empire of aristocrats promote such a belief system. So...Yes? Yes. I <i>personally </i> find that more interesting than there actually being a difference between Mnemnon and Nellens exaltation rates.<br /> <br /> Edit: AS for rate of Outcastes, yeah, I don't mind there being a large number of non-realm dragonblooded families, with the Realm's larger share coming from active efforts to incorporate existing states and recruit lost eggs more than their actual eugencis program having any validity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the above fellow. This does not make sense if it makes no difference and Breeding does not affect Exaltation rate. That's literally one of the DB schticks. Much like how Solars are 'I'm better than you in everything I put effort in and I'm also a shiny Ubersmench who makes my own morality' and 'I am the god king!', and how Alchemicals are 'Power to the state!', DBs are 'I am descended from heroes by blood and family, and their power lives in me!'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T08:22:20-08:00","id":1432792,"title":"","content":"My interpretation \u200bis that it is less that House Nellens has appreciably <i>worse</i> Dragon-Blooded than the other Great Houses, so much as there\u2019s a steep drop-off in the marriage prospects for their mortal dynasts.<br /> <br /> For the other Great Houses it\u2019s an acknowledged fact that the Terrestrial Exaltation skips generations and that\u2019s disappointing but has the advantage of them being much more controllable. Your mortal daughter paired with a good spouse might bring more Dragon-Blooded children into the House than her older sister whose professed her one true love to be the battlefield. <br /> <br /> However, when it happens to House Nellens? That\u2019s a reminder that they're patricians playing at being a Great House.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T09:30:09-08:00","id":1432796,"title":"","content":"I think the core topic is still vital and distinct enough that arguments about Dragon Blooded heredity ought to be spun off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T11:27:12-08:00","id":1432931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432792#post1432792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My interpretation \u200bis that it is less that House Nellens has appreciably <i>worse</i> Dragon-Blooded than the other Great Houses</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's anything in the 3e material indicating that pedigree has any effect on the power and potential of the Dragon-Blooded. The intention is that while a Dynast has better odds of having Dragon-Blooded offspring than an outcaste, the Dynast and the outcaste have the same potential to develop and manifest their own personal Exalted talents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T18:30:41-08:00","id":1432987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432746#post1432746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it might be cool if an Abyssal's redemption quest involved learning from the magic of the different types of Exalted, for which the Caul pilgrimage handles &quot;learning from&quot; Lunars, DBs, or both, but who also has to go on an incredibly difficult quest to a location important to Solars, an incredibly difficult quest to a location important to Sidereals, and maybe some others. Like needing help from all your friends to redeem yourself, but on a more cosmic scale.<br /> <br /> I also think what Moss said is very cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a fine <i>optional idea </i>for something for a Storyteller to offer for an Abyssal story arc, but I think it would be best in general to not have a <i>specific</i><i>, defined</i> route that becomes the Norm as a result, both because redemption becomes some expected standard route and because &quot;go hit the caul and do the other checklist of things' becomes a stale, boring set of tasks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T10:48:33-08:00","id":1433069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1432470-non-dragon-blooded-on-the-caul-pilgrimage?p=1432987#post1432987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is a fine <i>optional idea </i>for something for a Storyteller to offer for an Abyssal story arc, but I think it would be best in general to not have a <i>specific</i><i>, defined</i> route that becomes the Norm as a result, both because redemption becomes some expected standard route and because &quot;go hit the caul and do the other checklist of things' becomes a stale, boring set of tasks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that's why I said &quot;an Abyssal's redemption quest&quot; and not &quot;every single Abyssal's redemption quest&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T21:53:14-08:00","id":1433219,"title":"","content":"The Caul is a super-cool wild continent infused with ancient Primordial energies, recovered from the Wyld, and controlled by Lunars . Surely there's room for Solar, Abyssal, even Lunar sacred places and rituals of power that aren't the Dragon-Blooded pilgrimage route? Jerusalem has many holy places to Jews, Christians, and Muslims; some are only sacred to one of the traditions, some are sacred to multiple groups owing to shared heritage, and some are holy to more than one group but for different *reasons*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}